WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.804
Chapter 3 lists what Microsoft
Learn's material leaves to you,

2
00:00:03.804 --> 00:00:05.038
and what the kit adds.

3
00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.962
Each row is pinned by a test.

4
00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:11.722
The agent, the extension and the Entra
setting are three resources and one setting,

5
00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:15.222
so an instance with two of the
three looks ready in the portal;

6
00:00:15.222 --> 00:00:18.301
the kit reads all three, and
names whatever is missing.

7
00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:22.369
The category rules are in the
data platform book, not in Learn,

8
00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:27.495
so a pre-2022 instance or a cluster could
be scheduled for Arc work it can't use;

9
00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:30.913
the kit puts it in Category
3 before Arc is looked at.

10
00:00:30.913 --> 00:00:35.601
Resource Graph returns nothing, not an
error, for what the caller can't read,

11
00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:39.290
so the kit reports the agent
as not installed and keeps the

12
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.825
instance in Category 2, and
Lab 2 checks the sign-in first.

13
00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:44.642
The cloud is a sign-in choice,

14
00:00:44.642 --> 00:00:48.513
so the kit refuses a snapshot
from any cloud but Azure Cloud.

15
00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:52.303
And the managed identity
method is SQL Server 2025's:

16
00:00:52.303 --> 00:00:55.370
a 2022 instance recorded
that way gets a note.
